agent: An accepted implementation, “Northwind Restock Alerts,” already exists for this architecture. A separate realization can still be proposed.
  **Here is a proposed starting point for your implementation:**
  **Title:** Scheduled Restock Alert Service
  **Summary:** A GitHub Actions scheduled workflow runs every Monday, queries stock and reorder points from the order service using a read-only token, and emails one restock alert to the warehouse lead.
  **Realizations:**
  - **Scheduler:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow starts the check every Monday.
  - **Stock reader:** Calls the order service’s read-only stock query.
  - **Alert sender:** Filters items at or below their reorder point and sends one email listing them to the warehouse lead.
  **Deployment:** Hosted GitHub Actions runner.
  **Data:** Stock levels and reorder points flow from the order service to the workflow; no customer or payment data is handled.
  **Security:** The workflow uses a read-only stock-query token stored in GitHub Actions secrets.
  **Operations:** Runs weekly through GitHub Actions and depends on the order service’s accepted monthly availability target.
  **Deployed by:** GitHub Actions
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify can use GitHub Actions to get Scheduled Restock Alert Service up and running.
  **Managed by:** GitHub Actions
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify can use GitHub Actions for managing Scheduled Restock Alert Service once it’s running.
  **Language:** None
  **Why it matters:** This is a workflow/platform realization rather than a coding project covered by a listed language standard.
  **Capabilities:**
  - **Weekly restock alert:** Realized by GitHub Actions and email notification.
  - **Reorder point check:** Realized by the order service stock query and workflow filtering.
  **What would you add, correct, or remove?**
  If this is accurate, just say so.
